  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 7505.12 Failure to Pay an Agreement with a Creditor.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 264:11, a debtor who fails to pay any installment as specified in an agreement with a creditor shall have their license, driving privileges, and registration suspended. Upon receipt of notification of non-payment of agreement, the financial responsibility administrator shall issue a suspension order effective 10 days subsequent to the date of the notice. The notice shall advise the recipient of their right to request a hearing.\n\n(b) The scope of the hearing shall be limited to:\n\n(1) Whether the recipient entered into a security release agreement with the aggrieved party or parties; and\n\n(2) Whether the recipient is in compliance with the agreement.\n\nSource. #6337, eff 9-25-96 (from Saf-C 207.11); amd by #7349, eff 8-22-00; amd by #8174, INTERIM, eff 9-25-04, EXPIRES: 3-24-05; ss by #8230-B, eff 12-17-04; ss by #10395-B, eff 8-15-13; ss by #13938, eff 4-24-24 (formerly Saf-C 208.12) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 7500)",
